From 3941e273ad372bd2e9060daf5fddebd90e0e4f55 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marie-222 <289302950+marie-222@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:34:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] text-backend: add zwp_text_input_manager_v3, served by
 the input-method-v1 machinery

A text-input-v3 client (kitty, GTK4, Qt6...) is mapped to an internal text_input that activates the
input_method_context of the bound zwp_input_method_v1 client (e.g. fcitx5): enable/commit become
activate/surrounding_text/content_type/commit_state, preedit_string/commit_string/delete_surrounding_text
of the context become text-input-v3 events followed by done. enter/leave follow the keyboard focus.

[input-method] allow-any-client=true lets any client bind zwp_input_method_v1 instead of only the one
that weston started itself.
